<Base title="Projects — Rocket Cacique">
  <h1>Projects</h1>
  <p class="quiet">Things built on my own time, in my own repos.</p>

  <h2>open-code-review</h2>
  <p>
    An open-source CLI that reviews code changes with an LLM and applies fixes autonomously.
    I contributed AWS Bedrock as a built-in provider with native SigV4 auth, so it runs against
    Bedrock without an API-key middleman.
  </p>

  <h2>Alarm panel, resurrected</h2>
  <p>
    My house came with a 1990s DSC alarm panel. Rather than rip it out, I put an ESP32 on it —
    and when the panel itself finally died, pivoted to reading the zone wiring directly.
    Perfboard, end-of-line resistors, and documentation discipline: every dead end is written down.
  </p>

  <h2>A resume as code</h2>
  <p>
    Four targeted resume versions kept as Markdown sources of truth, built into HTML, Word, and
    LaTeX with pandoc and one small script. Diffable, reviewable, and no more "resume_final_v7.docx".
  </p>

  <p class="quiet">
    More on <a href="https://github.com/luisrodriguezcosme">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
